    "lawCode": "Amd §446, R & SS L",
    "lawSection": "Retirement and Social Security Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9069\n\nSPONSOR: JACKSON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the retirement and social security law, in relation to\nproviding for the transfer of service credit between certain retirement\nsystems\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo ensure that Tier 2 police officers in the New York City Police\nPension Fund (NYPPF) who transfer prior non-police service from the New\nYork City Employees' Retirement System (NYCERS) receive the same retire-\nment eligibility credit as those transferring service from the New York\nState and Local Retirement System (NYSLRS), eliminating an inequity in\npension credit.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends paragraph 2 of subdivision c of section 513 of the\nretirement and social security law by adding a new subparagraph (v) to:\n\n1. Make a member of the New York city police pension fund subject to\nthis article eligible to obtain credit for any period of service\nrendered as an assistant district attorney of a county within the city\nof New York and/or as an examining attorney for the New York City\nCommission to Combat Police Corruption which precedes service in the\nuniformed force of the New York city police department.\n\n2. Such service shall be deemed to be in service of the uniformed force\nof the New York city police department for purposes of eligibility for\nbenefits and to determine the amount of benefits under the New York city\npolice pension fund, provided that such member pays or transfers into\nthe New York city police pension fund all member contributions set forth\nin section five hundred seventeen of this article plus interest, at a\nrate of five percent per annum.\n\n3. For a member who transfers such contributions from the New York city\nemployees' retirement system to the New York city police pension fund or\nfor a member who withdraws such contributions from the New York city\nemployees' retirement system, such member's membership in the New York\ncity employees' retirement system shall cease upon such transfer or\nwithdrawal and such member shall retain no credited service in such\nsystem.\n\nSection 2 sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill seeks to remedy a glaring inequity facing current police offi-\ncers in NYPPF Tier 2 who have prior non-police New York City service\ntransferred from NYCERS to the PPF. These Tier 2 members are eligible\nfor a full-service retirement benefit of half their final salary upon\ncompletion of 20 years, however, prior non-police service transferred\nfrom NYCERS is currently credited towards retirement allowance rather\nthan the years needed for retirement eligibility.\n\n\nCurrently, New York City, through the PPF, has permitted Tier 2 police\nofficers to apply prior non-police New York State service from the New\nYork State and Local Retirement System (NYSLRS) to be credited towards\nretirement eligibility. Upon transfer or buyback, NYSLRS credit is\ndeemed as allowable police service and applied towards the 20 years\nrequired for service retirement. NYSLRS titles include non-police and\nclerical positions previously held with New York State. Since police\nofficers with prior New York State non-police service are permitted to\ntransfer NYSLRS credit and have it deemed as allowable police service,\nthose police officers with prior New York City non-police service who\ntransfer NYCERS credit should be granted the same benefit. This bill\nwill eliminate any distinction and cure the gross inequity between non-\npolice pension transfers between NYSLRS and NYCERS as it applies to Tier\n2 PPF members.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2025 - S.6437/ A. 7403 - Vetoed by the Governor - Memo 149\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nSee Fiscal Note.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
